      "content": "That's a fair point about LCC being more organic. My actual anxiety is the \"chaos\" factor. In some of these bundles, the contents are so fragmented and seemingly random that it feels less like a collection and more like a disorganized mess. Is there a risk that a highly granular system will actually struggle with this kind of deep fragmentation, or do these classification frameworks have specific protocols for managing items that seem to defy a logical structure during the initial sort?",
